It sucks in mazes, and it sucks at the castle relative to just using
the drawbridge.  It's nice at Ludios if you do that, but I'm not sure
that I've done Ludios more than 1-2 times (if even that) in my games
on NAO--by the time you can do it safely, there's just not that much
to be gained there.  I supposed extreme combat/spellcasting ability +
reflection + no MR + a gray dragon might make it worthwile,but I'd
rather just clear the Castle and wish up my MR.  The chance of a
throne wish/genocide isn't really worth the time.  If you enjoy those
big combats then it's worth it just for the fun; for me, Castle+Valley
fills that need, but that's purely personal and if you like it then
it's worth doing (pretty much by definition).

Obviously for a conduct game things change and Ludios might be more
worthwile, but I almost never even know whether the portal there
exists or not in a given game.



